    ('534be542-de80-4381-ac6a-70518e1768fa', 'ancona', 'Ancona', 'Ancona', true, 'Layers', 'Ancona chickens originated in Italy and were developed during nineteenth century. They were developed around the port of Ancona and later refined as an active Mediterranean layer. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

