    ('f19d41bd-0bd2-4fe3-a442-04b381ffc4fc', 'andalusian-blue', 'Andalusian - Blue', 'Andalusian - Blue', true, 'Layers', 'Andalusian chickens originated in Spain and were developed during nineteenth century. They were developed in Andalusia and exported to Britain and the United States as a blue-plumaged Mediterranean fowl. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

