    ('f52a817b-843a-4ca5-a5be-e80c981a200f', 'bantam-cochin-black', 'Bantam Cochin - Black', 'Bantam Cochin - Black', true, 'Bantams', 'Cochin chickens originated in China and were developed during nineteenth century. They were introduced to the West during the era of ''hen fever'' and developed primarily for size, feathering, and exhibition. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

