    ('d54aa073-4581-4247-8e06-a87707b140d3', 'cornish-cross', 'Cornish Cross', 'Cornish Cross', true, 'Meat Birds', 'Cornish Cross chickens were developed through the twentieth-century commercial broiler industry from Cornish-derived male and White Plymouth Rock-derived female lines. The line was selected for rapid growth, feed efficiency, and a broad breast, giving small farms and direct-market producers an alternative suited to its intended production system. Because commercial breeding programs can change, performance should be understood as a researched range rather than a permanent breed standard.

