    ('31a64e23-da3e-42cc-a37b-7707724b4882', 'delaware', 'Delaware', 'Delaware', true, 'Dual Purpose', 'Delaware chickens originated in United States and were developed during 1940s. They were developed by George Ellis in Delaware from sports appearing in New Hampshire and Barred Plymouth Rock broiler crosses. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

