    ('98b3f16a-c513-4934-9620-9de13992d6b3', 'modern-game-bantam', 'Modern Game Bantam', 'Modern Game Bantam', true, 'Bantams', 'Modern Game Bantam chickens originated in England and were developed during late nineteenth century. They were developed after cockfighting was prohibited by reshaping game-fowl ancestry into a highly upright exhibition bantam. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

