    ('87b08b50-6ed5-4526-9ac5-03f02889fea2', 'nankin', 'Nankin', 'Nankin', true, 'Bantams', 'Nankin chickens originated in Southeast Asia and England and were developed during centuries ago. They were preserved as one of the oldest true bantams and used in the development of several later bantam breeds. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

