    ('857de918-f979-450d-88be-b763b41da949', 'new-hampshire', 'New Hampshire', 'New Hampshire', true, 'Dual Purpose', 'New Hampshire chickens originated in United States and were developed during early twentieth century. They were developed from Rhode Island Red stock selected in New Hampshire for faster growth, early maturity, and practical production. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

