    ('18f67b7c-b751-4040-ac63-5948f3b1bcb8', 'rosecomb-black', 'Rosecomb - Black', 'Rosecomb - Black', true, 'Bantams', 'Rosecomb chickens originated in England and were developed during centuries ago. They were preserved as an old true bantam and refined for exhibition around its large rose comb and elegant outline. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

