    ('8a9bd37d-f6e0-40f5-9012-dbbf28e35b48', 'spanish-white-faced-black', 'Spanish - White Faced Black', 'Spanish - White Faced Black', true, 'Layers', 'White-Faced Black Spanish chickens originated in Spain and were developed during centuries ago. They were developed from old Mediterranean white-egg fowl and refined for its dramatic white facial skin. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

