    ('817ebe0b-afa4-4949-a4fe-1d5255561385', 'vorwerk', 'Vorwerk', 'Vorwerk', true, 'Layers', 'Vorwerk chickens originated in Germany and were developed during early twentieth century. They were created by Oskar Vorwerk to combine practical utility with a distinctive belted color pattern. Their history reflects the practical and cultural priorities of the farmers and breeders who maintained them before modern poultry production narrowed the number of commonly used breeds.

