    ('0862136d-155a-4be1-975a-92501c18839c', 'whiting-creole-blue', 'Whiting Creole Blue', 'Whiting Creole Blue', true, 'Specialty / Project', 'Whiting Creole Blue is a Whiting Farms specialty blue-egg line. Unlike a standardized heritage breed, the name identifies a commercial cross, strain, or breeding program selected for a practical production goal. Exact parent lines and performance can change between suppliers or generations, so catalog facts describe the type generally rather than guaranteeing identical birds from every source.

Whiting Creole Blue are Specialty / Project kept primarily for egg production. Hens generally lay large blue eggs, typically 200–250 eggs per year. Their single standardized temperament is variable, reflecting the expected catalog-level tendency while acknowledging individual and line variation. Buyers should confirm supplier-specific performance when production consistency matters. Egg output changes with age, season, nutrition, lighting, health, and management, so the production figure is a practical range rather than a guarantee.', null, 'blue', '200_250', 'Variable', true),
    ('fdadc55f-09e8-4a4c-974e-46f43ae7a2c4', 'whiting-green', 'Whiting Green', 'Whiting Green', true, 'Specialty / Project', 'Whiting Green is a Whiting Farms specialty green-egg line. Unlike a standardized heritage breed, the name identifies a commercial cross, strain, or breeding program selected for a practical production goal. Exact parent lines and performance can change between suppliers or generations, so catalog facts describe the type generally rather than guaranteeing identical birds from every source.

